# WHETHER keyring->auth() FITS ON THIS PART, and nothing else.
#
# os/inferno/init/armv7mauth.b runs authchk(1)'s pipe form: both ends of
# the exchange in one kernel, no radio.  authchk's own man page says
# that is the test everything else rests on -- "if it does not fit over
# a pipe it will not fit over a radio, and the radio would have been the
# expensive way to find out" -- and it had only been run on an
# mps2-an386.
#
# This image exists because the SHELL image cannot hold $Keyring.
# Declaring that module costs 197K of flash, measured, and armv7minit is
# already within 6K of bin2ihex's limit.  This one carries authchk, the
# two Authinfos, and no shell, no radio and no AX.25.
XIPDIS=\
	authchk.dis\


# The identities, which are NOT in the conf's root section: they belong
# to this image and to nothing else, and mkradiokeys(1) says why the
# signer's own key must never be on a board -- a satellite that can mint
# identities can be made to trust anything.
EXTRAROOT=\
	/dis/authchk.dis	/dis32/authchk.dis\
	/keys/ground		/keys/ground\
	/keys/satellite		/keys/satellite\

# Four.  The init is one, authchk spawns one end of the exchange and
# runs the other itself, and the kernel keeps a couple.  No #a, so none
# of the three kprocs a packet device starts.
NPROC=4

# auth is 1024-bit arithmetic and the heap is where libmp's temporaries
# live, so this split is the opposite of the station's: main carries no
# exportfs buffers and no AX.25 window here.
MAINPCNT=49
HEAPPCNT=50
IMAGEPCNT=1
